    "https://www.carthage.edu/why-carthage/career-preparation/": {
      "title": "Info For…",
      "description": "Career Preparation & Internships • Why Carthage • Carthage College Athletics Arts News & Events Giving Campus Tools The Bridge People Directory Office Directory Library/IT OneLogin Request Info Apply Visit Toggle Site Search Academics Admission & Aid Why Carthage Full Menu Close Full Menu Academics Majors & Minors What Should I Study? Graduate Programs Dual-Degree Programs Adult & Evening Programs Carthage Curriculum Study Abroad Experiential Learning Advising & Support Calendars & Schedules Admission & Aid Apply to Carthage Costs, Scholarships & Aid Visit Carthage Request Information Virtual Tour Contact Admissions Admissions Events Welcome, Accepted Students! Deposit Now! Why Carthage Exploration & Mentorship Career Preparation & Internships 4-Year Graduation Guarantee Affordability Our Faculty Commitment to Equity & Inclusion Opportunities Abroad Student Athletics Rankings & Honors Hear From Students My Carthage View Life at Carthage Housing & Residence Life Commuting to Carthage Dining Spiritual Life Student Activities Kenosha & Beyond Health, Wellness, & Safety Campus Services Aspire Career Preparation Engagement & Inclusion Arrival & Orientation About Carthage at a Glance Mission & Values College History Facilities Location & Map Offices & Services Divisions, Centers & Institutes Accreditation Directory Search Submit Info For… Current Students Alumni Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Community Athletics Arts News & Events Giving Request Info Apply Visit Instagram Twitter Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Flickr Merit Pages Close Search Search Search Keyword Submit Career Preparation & Internships Home Why Carthage Career Preparation & Internships Why Carthage Exploration & Mentorship Career Preparation & Internships 4-Year Graduation Guarantee Affordability Our Faculty Commitment to Equity & Inclusion Opportunities Abroad Student Athletics Rankings & Honors Hear From Students My Carthage View ENTRANCE RAMP TO SUCCESS Built exclusively for Carthage students, The Aspire Program connects interests to hidden career paths as you grow into a versatile professional who’s equipped to handle anything. All students participate, and we spread the tasks across four years so it won’t stress you out. Think of it as a guided pathway to a great job and, even better, a rewarding life. Shape Your Future Entering The Aspire Program, students start shaping a customized career plan in their first days on campus. Here are a few of the highlights: Make Connections Based on your interests, we’ll match you with a career specialist who knows the industry inside and out. Plus, it’s easy to network with Carthage graduates working in similar fields. You can even attend a professional conference without leaving campus. Learn by Doing Valuable hands-on experience can give you an early edge in the competitive job market. Internships: Our prime location between Milwaukee and Chicago puts internships with all kinds of companies and organizations within reach. If you find a great opportunity that just doesn’t pay enough, Carthage has funding available. Study Abroad: Whether they learn overseas for a year, a semester, or just a few weeks through our popular J-Term study tours, students consistently return transformed. Research: Here, original research is part of every student’s journey. Faculty in the sciences lead experiments with big-time partners like NASA, but all majors require a scholarly project to graduate. Internships provide hands-on learning at companies like Snap-On, Jockey, Abbott Laboratories, Fiserv Forum, and more! Carthage space science students have interned at the NASA Kennedy Space Center and at the NASA Academy at NASA Langley Research Center. It’s not just about getting a great job. The Aspire Program is about understanding how your activities in and outside of work can help you to build a satisfying life. Early and often in their time at Carthage, students are challenged to perform original study under the close guidance of experienced faculty. Carthage hosts several events throughout the year, including career fairs and networking opportunities, so students can learn more about available internship, grad school, and career prep opportunities. › Previous slide › Next slide MORE ABOUT THE ASPIRE PROGRAM “The Aspire Program has been a helpful resource in preparing me for a career. The staff have supported me with resume reviews, career advice, and guidance on professional development.” — Ryan Fuentes ’28 Gain opportunities through Carthage professors Thanks to Carthage’s small class sizes, students build strong connections with professors who actively support them in landing internships and jobs. Meet Carthage professors who help students land jobs Start Exploring Explore Majors And Careers Have A Plan From Day One Why Carthage? Exploration & Mentorship 4-Year Graduation Guarantee Opportunities Abroad 2001 Alford Park Drive Kenosha, WI 53140 (262) 551-8500 Contact Map & Directions Request Info Apply Visit Carthage Give Light that Travels | The Campaign For Carthage Athletics Bookstore Library/IT OneLogin The Bridge Virtual Tour Work at Carthage #carthageviews Instagram Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Merit Pages TikTok © Carthage College Privacy Policy Non-Discrimination Statement Policies Title IX This website uses cookies to measure traffic and improve your experience. Declining tracking cookies will set a single cookie to remember your preference. You can learn more by visiting our Privacy Policy . Accept Decline"
    },
    "https://www.carthage.edu/why-carthage/our-faculty/": {
      "title": "Carthage Faculty: Devoted to Teaching",
      "description": "Our Faculty • Why Carthage • Carthage College Athletics Arts News & Events Giving Campus Tools The Bridge People Directory Office Directory Library/IT OneLogin Request Info Apply Visit Toggle Site Search Academics Admission & Aid Why Carthage Full Menu Close Full Menu Academics Majors & Minors What Should I Study? Graduate Programs Dual-Degree Programs Adult & Evening Programs Carthage Curriculum Study Abroad Experiential Learning Advising & Support Calendars & Schedules Admission & Aid Apply to Carthage Costs, Scholarships & Aid Visit Carthage Request Information Virtual Tour Contact Admissions Admissions Events Welcome, Accepted Students! Deposit Now! Why Carthage Exploration & Mentorship Career Preparation & Internships 4-Year Graduation Guarantee Affordability Our Faculty Commitment to Equity & Inclusion Opportunities Abroad Student Athletics Rankings & Honors Hear From Students My Carthage View Life at Carthage Housing & Residence Life Commuting to Carthage Dining Spiritual Life Student Activities Kenosha & Beyond Health, Wellness, & Safety Campus Services Aspire Career Preparation Engagement & Inclusion Arrival & Orientation About Carthage at a Glance Mission & Values College History Facilities Location & Map Offices & Services Divisions, Centers & Institutes Accreditation Directory Search Submit Info For… Current Students Alumni Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Community Athletics Arts News & Events Giving Request Info Apply Visit Instagram Twitter Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Flickr Merit Pages Close Search Search Search Keyword Submit Our Faculty Home Why Carthage Our Faculty Why Carthage Exploration & Mentorship Career Preparation & Internships 4-Year Graduation Guarantee Affordability Our Faculty Commitment to Equity & Inclusion Opportunities Abroad Student Athletics Rankings & Honors Hear From Students My Carthage View Carthage Faculty: Devoted to Teaching Passion for teaching is hard to quantify. But you’ll see it. 100% of classes taught by faculty (not TAs) Like when class ends, and your professor refuses to leave until you get it. Or when their lunch break becomes your mock interview. Or when you skip class and find a concerned email waiting in your inbox. Passion is in their job description. It’s contagious. And it’s why our professors will encourage you as often as they challenge you. Their enthusiasm for your success in college and beyond makes Carthage a very special place. They cheer at athletic and cultural events, and will know you well enough to write stellar letters of recommendation to help you to that next step after graduation. Ask your admissions representative to introduce you to more professors during your campus visit . You can also learn more about our faculty by visiting our academic program websites . Professor Pascal Rollet (modern languages) and students on a Paris J-Term study tour. Professor Edward Kawakami and the Carthage Philharmonic . Professor Thomas Carr ( biology , paleontology ) holds a portion of a shin and ankle of a T. rex . Professor John Kirk ( chemistry ) Professor Maggie Burk ( music ) and the Carthage Choir . Professor Jojin Van Winkle ( art , photography , and film and new media ) Professor Michele Hancock ( education ), Vice President of College Culture for Inclusion Professor Angela Dassow ( biology ) Professor Carter Rockhill ( management , marketing , and Master of Business — Design and Innovation and Sports Management ) Professor Christine Blaine ( chemistry ) Professor Erik Kulke (modern languages, Director of Study Abroad ) Professor Matt Zorn ( geographic information science , geoscience ) Profs. Jeff Roberg ( political science ) and Maribel Morales (modern languages) in Peru on a J-Term study tour. Professor Nina Weisling ( education ) was selected by the Class of 2023 to be the faculty speaker at the 2023 Commencement Ceremony. Anthony Barnhart , associate professor of psychological science and Carthage’s resident magician Professor Laura Huaracha ( graphic design ) Professor Wenjie Sun ( geographic information science , computer science , Asian studies ) › Previous slide › Next slide “The faculty here are incredibly talented and also genuinely supportive. They make it clear that they want every student to succeed. I’ve been able to go to my teachers for help with everything from managing a busy schedule to working through challenging material, and they’ve always taken the time to guide me. Those relationships have made a big difference in helping me stay on track and grow both academically and personally.” — Grace Grassinger ’29 Keep Exploring Exploration & Mentorship 4-Year Graduation Guarantee Opportunities Abroad 2001 Alford Park Drive Kenosha, WI 53140 (262) 551-8500 Contact Map & Directions Request Info Apply Visit Carthage Give Light that Travels | The Campaign For Carthage Athletics Bookstore Library/IT OneLogin The Bridge Virtual Tour Work at Carthage #carthageviews Instagram Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Merit Pages TikTok © Carthage College Privacy Policy Non-Discrimination Statement Policies Title IX This website uses cookies to measure traffic and improve your experience. Declining tracking cookies will set a single cookie to remember your preference. You can learn more by visiting our Privacy Policy . Accept Decline"
    },
    "https://www.carthage.edu/life-at-carthage/aspire/": {
      "title": "Info For…",
      "description": "The Aspire Program: Career & Professional Development • Carthage College Athletics Arts News & Events Giving Campus Tools The Bridge People Directory Office Directory Library/IT OneLogin Request Info Apply Visit Toggle Site Search Academics Admission & Aid Why Carthage Full Menu Close Full Menu Academics Majors & Minors What Should I Study? Graduate Programs Dual-Degree Programs Adult & Evening Programs Carthage Curriculum Study Abroad Experiential Learning Advising & Support Calendars & Schedules Admission & Aid Apply to Carthage Costs, Scholarships & Aid Visit Carthage Request Information Virtual Tour Contact Admissions Admissions Events Welcome, Accepted Students! Deposit Now! Why Carthage Exploration & Mentorship Career Preparation & Internships 4-Year Graduation Guarantee Affordability Our Faculty Commitment to Equity & Inclusion Opportunities Abroad Student Athletics Rankings & Honors Hear From Students My Carthage View Life at Carthage Housing & Residence Life Commuting to Carthage Dining Spiritual Life Student Activities Kenosha & Beyond Health, Wellness, & Safety Campus Services Aspire Career Preparation Engagement & Inclusion Arrival & Orientation About Carthage at a Glance Mission & Values College History Facilities Location & Map Offices & Services Divisions, Centers & Institutes Accreditation Directory Search Submit Info For… Current Students Alumni Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Community Athletics Arts News & Events Giving Request Info Apply Visit Instagram Twitter Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Flickr Merit Pages Close Search Search Search Keyword Submit The Aspire Program: Career & Professional Development Home The Aspire Program: Career & Professional Development Career Preparation starting Day One The Aspire Program at Carthage is a multifaceted four-year career development sequence designed exclusively for Carthage students. Identify your interests and purpose and connect the dots to potential careers. The program prepares you for a meaningful life, no matter what the future holds. The Four-Year Plan <div class=\"lw_widget lw_widget_type_blockquote\"><blockquote class=\"blockquote\"><div class=\"blockquote__image\"><picture class=\"lw_image\"><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"/live/image/scale/2x/gid/17/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/0,70,570,639/41436_Kelvin-Madjinor-27.rev.1742413672.webp 2x, /live/image/scale/3x/gid/17/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/0,70,570,639/41436_Kelvin-Madjinor-27.rev.1742413672.webp 3x\" data-origin=\"responsive\"/><source type=\"image/jpeg\" srcset=\"/live/image/scale/2x/gid/17/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/0,70,570,639/41436_Kelvin-Madjinor-27.rev.1742413672.jpg 2x, /live/image/scale/3x/gid/17/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/0,70,570,639/41436_Kelvin-Madjinor-27.rev.1742413672.jpg 3x\" data-origin=\"responsive\"/><img src=\"/live/image/gid/17/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/0,70,570,639/41436_Kelvin-Madjinor-27.rev.1742413672.jpg\" alt=\"Kelvin Madjinor '27\" width=\"183\" height=\"183\" srcset=\"/live/image/scale/2x/gid/17/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/0,70,570,639/41436_Kelvin-Madjinor-27.rev.1742413672.jpg 2x, /live/image/scale/3x/gid/17/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/0,70,570,639/41436_Kelvin-Madjinor-27.rev.1742413672.jpg 3x\" data-max-w=\"570\" data-max-h=\"569\" loading=\"lazy\" data-optimized=\"true\"/></picture></div><div class=\"blockquote__content\"><div class=\"blockquote__quote\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"icon icon-round-left-quote\" width=\"48\" height=\"33\"><use xlink:href=\"#icon-round-left-quote\"/></svg><p>  “With the help of The Aspire Program staff, I’ve created a resume and gained connections with alumni.”</p></div><footer class=\"blockquote__footer\"><span class=\"blockquote__author\"><a href=\"/live/profiles/3008-kelvin-madjinor\">Kelvin Madjinor</a> ’27</span></footer></div></blockquote></div> <div class=\"lw_widget lw_widget_type_blockquote\"><blockquote class=\"blockquote\"><div class=\"blockquote__image\"><picture class=\"lw_image\"><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"/live/image/scale/2x/gid/12/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/479,319,1547,1388/43811_29811_171052831004161.rev.1778689185.webp 2x, /live/image/scale/3x/gid/12/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/479,319,1547,1388/43811_29811_171052831004161.rev.1778689185.webp 3x\" data-origin=\"responsive\"/><source type=\"image/jpeg\" srcset=\"/live/image/scale/2x/gid/12/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/479,319,1547,1388/43811_29811_171052831004161.rev.1778689185.jpg 2x, /live/image/scale/3x/gid/12/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/479,319,1547,1388/43811_29811_171052831004161.rev.1778689185.jpg 3x\" data-origin=\"responsive\"/><img src=\"/live/image/gid/12/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/479,319,1547,1388/43811_29811_171052831004161.rev.1778689185.jpg\" alt=\"Evan Reinemann '28\" width=\"183\" height=\"183\" srcset=\"/live/image/scale/2x/gid/12/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/479,319,1547,1388/43811_29811_171052831004161.rev.1778689185.jpg 2x, /live/image/scale/3x/gid/12/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/479,319,1547,1388/43811_29811_171052831004161.rev.1778689185.jpg 3x\" data-max-w=\"1068\" data-max-h=\"1069\" loading=\"lazy\" data-optimized=\"true\"/></picture></div><div class=\"blockquote__content\"><div class=\"blockquote__quote\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"icon icon-round-left-quote\" width=\"48\" height=\"33\"><use xlink:href=\"#icon-round-left-quote\"/></svg><p>  “The Aspire Program has played an important role in preparing me for my career by offering resources such as job search assistance, resume building, and free professional headshots.”</p></div><footer class=\"blockquote__footer\"><span class=\"blockquote__author\"><a href=\"/live/profiles/3556-evan-reinemann\">Evan Reinemann</a> ’28</span></footer></div></blockquote></div> <div class=\"lw_widget lw_widget_type_blockquote\"><blockquote class=\"blockquote\"><div class=\"blockquote__image\"><picture class=\"lw_image\"><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"/live/image/scale/2x/gid/77/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/113,0,1364,1250/43192_28333_171052831004161.rev.1770318388.webp 2x, /live/image/scale/3x/gid/77/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/113,0,1364,1250/43192_28333_171052831004161.rev.1770318388.webp 3x\" data-origin=\"responsive\"/><source type=\"image/jpeg\" srcset=\"/live/image/scale/2x/gid/77/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/113,0,1364,1250/43192_28333_171052831004161.rev.1770318388.jpg 2x, /live/image/scale/3x/gid/77/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/113,0,1364,1250/43192_28333_171052831004161.rev.1770318388.jpg 3x\" data-origin=\"responsive\"/><img src=\"/live/image/gid/77/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/113,0,1364,1250/43192_28333_171052831004161.rev.1770318388.jpg\" alt=\"Ryan Fuentes '28\" width=\"183\" height=\"183\" srcset=\"/live/image/scale/2x/gid/77/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/113,0,1364,1250/43192_28333_171052831004161.rev.1770318388.jpg 2x, /live/image/scale/3x/gid/77/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/113,0,1364,1250/43192_28333_171052831004161.rev.1770318388.jpg 3x\" data-max-w=\"1251\" data-max-h=\"1250\" loading=\"lazy\" data-optimized=\"true\"/></picture></div><div class=\"blockquote__content\"><div class=\"blockquote__quote\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"icon icon-round-left-quote\" width=\"48\" height=\"33\"><use xlink:href=\"#icon-round-left-quote\"/></svg><p>  “The Aspire Program has been a helpful resource in preparing me for a career. The staff have supported me with resume reviews, career advice, and guidance on professional development.”</p></div><footer class=\"blockquote__footer\"><span class=\"blockquote__author\"><a href=\"/live/profiles/3411-ryan-fuentes\">Ryan Fuentes</a> ’28</span></footer></div></blockquote></div> <div class=\"lw_widget lw_widget_type_blockquote\"><blockquote class=\"blockquote\"><div class=\"blockquote__image\"><picture class=\"lw_image\"><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"/live/image/scale/2x/gid/47/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/0,531,2130,2661/43203_28389_171052831004161.rev.1770666165.webp 2x, /live/image/scale/3x/gid/47/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/0,531,2130,2661/43203_28389_171052831004161.rev.1770666165.webp 3x\" data-origin=\"responsive\"/><source type=\"image/jpeg\" srcset=\"/live/image/scale/2x/gid/47/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/0,531,2130,2661/43203_28389_171052831004161.rev.1770666165.jpg 2x, /live/image/scale/3x/gid/47/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/0,531,2130,2661/43203_28389_171052831004161.rev.1770666165.jpg 3x\" data-origin=\"responsive\"/><img src=\"/live/image/gid/47/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/0,531,2130,2661/43203_28389_171052831004161.rev.1770666165.jpg\" alt=\"Anita Gross '28\" width=\"183\" height=\"183\" srcset=\"/live/image/scale/2x/gid/47/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/0,531,2130,2661/43203_28389_171052831004161.rev.1770666165.jpg 2x, /live/image/scale/3x/gid/47/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/0,531,2130,2661/43203_28389_171052831004161.rev.1770666165.jpg 3x\" data-max-w=\"2130\" data-max-h=\"2130\" loading=\"lazy\" data-optimized=\"true\"/></picture></div><div class=\"blockquote__content\"><div class=\"blockquote__quote\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"icon icon-round-left-quote\" width=\"48\" height=\"33\"><use xlink:href=\"#icon-round-left-quote\"/></svg><p>  “The Aspire Program staff have helped me build an academic resume that looks professional and even taught me how to search for internships on LinkedIn.”</p></div><footer class=\"blockquote__footer\"><span class=\"blockquote__author\"><a href=\"/live/profiles/3413-anita-gross\">Anita Gross</a> ’28</span></footer></div></blockquote></div> <div class=\"lw_widget lw_widget_type_blockquote\"><blockquote class=\"blockquote\"><div class=\"blockquote__image\"><picture class=\"lw_image\"><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"/live/image/scale/2x/gid/77/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/563,1190,2400,3027/43201_28382_171052831004161.rev.1770663335.webp 2x, /live/image/scale/3x/gid/77/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/563,1190,2400,3027/43201_28382_171052831004161.rev.1770663335.webp 3x\" data-origin=\"responsive\"/><source type=\"image/jpeg\" srcset=\"/live/image/scale/2x/gid/77/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/563,1190,2400,3027/43201_28382_171052831004161.rev.1770663335.jpg 2x, /live/image/scale/3x/gid/77/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/563,1190,2400,3027/43201_28382_171052831004161.rev.1770663335.jpg 3x\" data-origin=\"responsive\"/><img src=\"/live/image/gid/77/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/563,1190,2400,3027/43201_28382_171052831004161.rev.1770663335.jpg\" alt=\"Joey Westphal '27\" width=\"183\" height=\"183\" srcset=\"/live/image/scale/2x/gid/77/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/563,1190,2400,3027/43201_28382_171052831004161.rev.1770663335.jpg 2x, /live/image/scale/3x/gid/77/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/563,1190,2400,3027/43201_28382_171052831004161.rev.1770663335.jpg 3x\" data-max-w=\"1837\" data-max-h=\"1837\" loading=\"lazy\" data-optimized=\"true\"/></picture></div><div class=\"blockquote__content\"><div class=\"blockquote__quote\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"icon icon-round-left-quote\" width=\"48\" height=\"33\"><use xlink:href=\"#icon-round-left-quote\"/></svg><p>  “The Aspire Program staff helped me create my resume, look for internships, and practice in mock interviews.”</p></div><footer class=\"blockquote__footer\"><span class=\"blockquote__author\"><a href=\"/live/profiles/3412-joey-westphal\">Joey Westphal</a> ’27</span></footer></div></blockquote></div> <div class=\"lw_widget lw_widget_type_blockquote\"><blockquote class=\"blockquote\"><div class=\"blockquote__image\"><picture class=\"lw_image\"><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"/live/image/scale/2x/gid/93/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/0,382,2316,2698/43167_28291_171052831004161.rev.1769540132.webp 2x, /live/image/scale/3x/gid/93/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/0,382,2316,2698/43167_28291_171052831004161.rev.1769540132.webp 3x\" data-origin=\"responsive\"/><source type=\"image/jpeg\" srcset=\"/live/image/scale/2x/gid/93/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/0,382,2316,2698/43167_28291_171052831004161.rev.1769540132.jpg 2x, /live/image/scale/3x/gid/93/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/0,382,2316,2698/43167_28291_171052831004161.rev.1769540132.jpg 3x\" data-origin=\"responsive\"/><img src=\"/live/image/gid/93/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/0,382,2316,2698/43167_28291_171052831004161.rev.1769540132.jpg\" alt=\"Makenzie Baker '27\" width=\"183\" height=\"183\" srcset=\"/live/image/scale/2x/gid/93/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/0,382,2316,2698/43167_28291_171052831004161.rev.1769540132.jpg 2x, /live/image/scale/3x/gid/93/width/183/height/183/crop/1/src_region/0,382,2316,2698/43167_28291_171052831004161.rev.1769540132.jpg 3x\" data-max-w=\"2316\" data-max-h=\"2316\" loading=\"lazy\" data-optimized=\"true\"/></picture></div><div class=\"blockquote__content\"><div class=\"blockquote__quote\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"icon icon-round-left-quote\" width=\"48\" height=\"33\"><use xlink:href=\"#icon-round-left-quote\"/></svg><p>  “I used The Aspire Program during my freshman year. My advisor helped me set up my resume and start building my experience.”</p></div><footer class=\"blockquote__footer\"><span class=\"blockquote__author\"><a href=\"/live/profiles/3396-makenzie-baker\">Makenzie Baker</a> ’27</span></footer></div></blockquote></div> About The Aspire Program At Carthage, all first-year students begin career development planning from their first days on campus. Through The Aspire Program, they develop a dynamic approach to goal-setting and life skill-building. Students will own their ability to be lifelong learners and impactful contributors in the world, and to recover when plans don’t go as expected. Launched in 2019, The Aspire Program builds on Carthage’s strong history of providing students with the skills they need to succeed. For Carthage Students Stories & Outcomes Employers & Community View {title} video embed Learn more about Carthage’s Aspire Program. Close YouTube Video: {title} Enable Javascript to view the video embed or view the video directly at https://youtube.com/watch?v=EGkcFp6359Q . Driving Student Success The Aspire Program at Carthage College is nationally recognized for its innovative approach to career development. With numerous awards, competitive grant support, and featured case studies, the program continues to lead in student success. See the Aspire Program’s Awards Hear from our employer partners “Partnering with Carthage College and The Aspire Program has been an incredibly rewarding experience. Their commitment to preparing students for life beyond the classroom is truly inspiring. The Aspire Program’s team is collaborative, responsive, and clearly passionate about creating meaningful connections between students and the professional world. I’ve been continually impressed by their innovative approach and the value they bring to both students and external partners.\" — Dulce Morales, Senior Lead, Community Relations and Business Development at BCU “Abbott Finance, Carthage College, and The Aspire Program have built a great relationship over the past few years. Abbott has been allowed to engage with students each year and present on career opportunities. In doing so, we’ve been able to recruit bright and driven talent from Carthage into our co-op/internship program and as full-time employees. We hope to continue to build upon this relationship in the future.” — Asif Choudhury, Sr. Finance Manager at Abbott “Carthage College is a distinguished institution for education, personal development, and career preparation. The collaboration between The Aspire Program and the Kenosha Police Department has thrived. We appreciate the dedication of Carthage interns at our department and their commitment to our city and organization. We are grateful for this partnership and eagerly anticipate offering more programs to strengthen our community together.” — Jason Tetrick, Lieutenant and Training Officer at Kenosha Police Department › Previous slide › Next slide Connect with Us Aspire Staff Find Your Career Specialist Handshake and Other Resources News from the Aspire Program News & Events 2001 Alford Park Drive Kenosha, WI 53140 (262) 551-8500 Contact Map & Directions Request Info Apply Visit Carthage Give Light that Travels | The Campaign For Carthage Athletics Bookstore Library/IT OneLogin The Bridge Virtual Tour Work at Carthage #carthageviews Instagram Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Merit Pages TikTok © Carthage College Privacy Policy Non-Discrimination Statement Policies Title IX This website uses cookies to measure traffic and improve your experience. Declining tracking cookies will set a single cookie to remember your preference. You can learn more by visiting our Privacy Policy . Accept Decline"
    },
    "https://www.carthage.edu/faculty-staff/": {
      "title": "Info For…",
      "description": "Info for Faculty & Staff • Info for Faculty & Staff • Carthage College Athletics Arts News & Events Giving Campus Tools The Bridge People Directory Office Directory Library/IT OneLogin Request Info Apply Visit Toggle Site Search Academics Admission & Aid Why Carthage Full Menu Close Full Menu Academics Majors & Minors What Should I Study? Graduate Programs Dual-Degree Programs Adult & Evening Programs Carthage Curriculum Study Abroad Experiential Learning Advising & Support Calendars & Schedules Admission & Aid Apply to Carthage Costs, Scholarships & Aid Visit Carthage Request Information Virtual Tour Contact Admissions Admissions Events Welcome, Accepted Students! Deposit Now! Why Carthage Exploration & Mentorship Career Preparation & Internships 4-Year Graduation Guarantee Affordability Our Faculty Commitment to Equity & Inclusion Opportunities Abroad Student Athletics Rankings & Honors Hear From Students My Carthage View Life at Carthage Housing & Residence Life Commuting to Carthage Dining Spiritual Life Student Activities Kenosha & Beyond Health, Wellness, & Safety Campus Services Aspire Career Preparation Engagement & Inclusion Arrival & Orientation About Carthage at a Glance Mission & Values College History Facilities Location & Map Offices & Services Divisions, Centers & Institutes Accreditation Directory Search Submit Info For… Current Students Alumni Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Community Athletics Arts News & Events Giving Request Info Apply Visit Instagram Twitter Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Flickr Merit Pages Close Search Search Search Keyword Submit Info for Faculty & Staff Home Info for Faculty & Staff Homepage Info for Faculty & Staff Staff Council Teaching Commons Faculty Meeting Schedule Faculty Committees Volunteer Program The Bridge Find news and info for the Carthage community. VIEW THE BRIDGE The following resources are intended to help Carthage faculty and staff quickly and easily find information you need. If you are unable to locate something, or if you have a suggestion to improve this resource list, please send an email to The Bridge, bridge@carthage.edu . Thank you! — Office of Marketing & Communications Quick Links to essentials: OneLogin Directory Carthage Email (Gmail) Working at Carthage Best bet: Human Resources website Quick links: Benefits information (log-in required) Careers at Carthage (Job Postings) Educational Assistance Program (log-in required) Employee Handbook Human Resources Order Business Cards Order Name Tags Payroll (log-in required) Policies: Campus Policies Policies: HR Policies & Procedures (log-in required) Recruitment & Staffing (log-in required) Staff Council Campus Services Quick links: The Bridge Campus Bookstore: Slingshot Building Hours Birdie Bucks Dining Options Fitness Facilities Key Requests Mailroom Services Maintenance Room Scheduling in AdAstra (access through OneLogin) Facilities & Event Management First stop for event planning: Event and Conference Services Website Learn more about reserving rooms, requesting catering, arranging for special event parking, and more on the Conference Services website. Carthage faculty and staff should click on “For Carthage Community Members” First stop for maintenance needs: Maintenance Request Form Complete a Work Order through the Facility Services Work Order Portal. Submit requests for room repairs, key and lock issues, cleaning services, moving offices/relocations, and more. If you have a maintenance emergency, call Facilities Management at 262-551-5752, or the Office of Public Safety on evenings and weekends, 262-551-5911. Quick links: Campus Map Event and Conference Services Environmental Services Event Policies Facilities Management (Campus Operations) Parking Policies Reserve a Room in AdAstra (access through OneLogin) Catering Submit a Maintenance Request Faculty Resources A note to our faculty colleagues: If there is a resource that is not listed in this section that should be, please let us know! Send the name of the resource to bridge@carthage.edu . We’ll work with the Office of the Provost to get it updated and listed as soon as possible. Thank you! Calendars & Schedules Academic Calendars & Schedules Class Period Times Faculty Meeting Schedule Final Exam Schedule Governance, Leadership & Policy Academic Senate (log-in required) Bylaws Committees (log-in required) Constitution Department and Program Chairs Department/Program Chairs Resource Guide Faculty Handbook Faculty Qualifications Policy | Faculty Qualifications Certification Form Faculty Search Guidelines Faculty Travel Policy Faculty Travel Request Form Provost’s Office Resources Assessing Student Learning Outcomes Course Proposal Form (log-in required) Institutional Review Board LibGuides: Adaptive Course Design Office of Sponsored Programs Reflection Toolkit Resources for Research Teaching Commons Marketing & Communications Support First stop: Office of Marketing & Communications website The “Mar-Comm” team’s primary mission is to support recruitment, retention, fundraising, and engagement. The team assists Carthage offices and departments with Carthage-branded merchandise, websites, brochures and other printed materials, photographs, media relations, and much more. Please contact us if you plan to design and produce ANY Carthage or Carthage Firebirds-branded items to avoid unnecessary expense. Quick links: Use the Project Request Form to request … Carthage merchandise/swag News Release Permission to use the Carthage or Carthage Firebirds logo Print or Design Project Website Update Update Your Online Profile Faculty Online Profiles: Update an existing profile | Request a new faculty profile Staff Online Profiles: Update or create a staff profile Purchasing & Finance First stop: Finance and Administrative Services website or Workday Finance and Administrative Services at Carthage assists faculty and staff with accounts payable, budgeting, and campus operations. Many actions for these processes are managed in Workday. Quick links: Expense transfer form Travel policies and travel request forms Safety & Support First stop: Office of Public Safety website Quick links: Bias Incident Report / Bias Education Response Team (BERT) Carthage Employee Assistance Program (log-in required) Campus Conduct Hotline (log-in required) Designated Tornado Shelters Emergency Management Procedures Guide Emergency Notification System Engagement and Inclusion Office of Public Safety Staff Council Title IX Tools, Technology & Computer Support First stop: Hedberg Library website Quick links: IT help After-Hours IT support Reset your password Register to use the Carthage network Media Services (Livestreaming, Classroom Technology, Educational Media) Request an update to a page on the Carthage.edu website 2001 Alford Park Drive Kenosha, WI 53140 (262) 551-8500 Contact Map & Directions Request Info Apply Visit Carthage Give Light that Travels | The Campaign For Carthage Athletics Bookstore Library/IT OneLogin The Bridge Virtual Tour Work at Carthage #carthageviews Instagram Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Merit Pages TikTok © Carthage College Privacy Policy Non-Discrimination Statement Policies Title IX This website uses cookies to measure traffic and improve your experience. Declining tracking cookies will set a single cookie to remember your preference. You can learn more by visiting our Privacy Policy . Accept Decline"
    },
