    "https://www.carthage.edu/live/news/57579-adjunct-assistant-professor-nursing": {
      "title": "Adjunct Assistant Professor, Nursing",
      "description": "Adjunct Assistant Professor, Nursing • Human Resources • Carthage College Athletics Arts News & Events Giving Campus Tools The Bridge People Directory Office Directory Library/IT OneLogin Request Info Apply Visit Toggle Site Search Academics Admission & Aid Why Carthage Full Menu Close Full Menu Academics Majors & Minors What Should I Study? Graduate Programs Dual-Degree Programs Adult & Evening Programs Carthage Curriculum Study Abroad Experiential Learning Advising & Support Calendars & Schedules Admission & Aid Apply to Carthage Costs, Scholarships & Aid Visit Carthage Request Information Virtual Tour Contact Admissions Admissions Events Welcome, Accepted Students! Deposit Now! Why Carthage Exploration & Mentorship Career Preparation & Internships 4-Year Graduation Guarantee Affordability Our Faculty Commitment to Equity & Inclusion Opportunities Abroad Student Athletics Rankings & Honors Hear From Students My Carthage View Life at Carthage Housing & Residence Life Commuting to Carthage Dining Spiritual Life Student Activities Kenosha & Beyond Health, Wellness, & Safety Campus Services Aspire Career Preparation Engagement & Inclusion Arrival & Orientation About Carthage at a Glance Mission & Values College History Facilities Location & Map Offices & Services Divisions, Centers & Institutes Accreditation Directory Search Submit Info For… Current Students Alumni Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Community Athletics Arts News & Events Giving Request Info Apply Visit Instagram Twitter Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Flickr Merit Pages Close Search Search Search Keyword Submit Adjunct Assistant Professor, Nursing Home Human Resources Adjunct Assistant Professor, Nursing All Stories June 08, 2026 Nancy Reese; nreese@carthage.edu Share on Facebook Share on Twitter Share on LinkedIn Share via Email The Nursing Department at Carthage College invites applications for an Adjunct Assistant Professor of Nursing position starting August 15, 2026. Applications will be accepted on a rolling basis until positions are filled. Key Responsibilities: Instruction: Teach undergraduate students in skills labs, simulation labs, and clinical organizations. Evaluation: Provide both formative (ongoing) and summative (final) student performance reviews. Mentorship: Help students connect classroom theory to hands-on clinical practice. Development: Guide students in building critical thinking and clinical judgment skills. Alignment: Follow the philosophy, mission, and values of the Nursing Department. Minimum Qualifications: Education: Master’s degree in Nursing (MSN). Experience: Minimum 2 years of clinical nursing experience in a relevant field. Licensure: Unencumbered Wisconsin RN license and Illinois licensure if needed. Clearances: Must pass a criminal history and background check. Certifications: Up-to-date CPR certification and required immunizations. Knowledge: Deep understanding of health assessments, medications, treatments, and diagnoses. Application Process: Deadlines: Applications are accepted on a rolling basis until positions are filled. Required Documents: Submit a cover letter and resume via the application portal’s “Resume Upload” section. Inquiries: Direct questions to Nancy Reese via email at NReese@Carthage.edu . Apply Online About Carthage Located on the shore of Lake Michigan in the thriving Chicago-Milwaukee corridor, Carthage College blends the best liberal arts traditions with desirable degree programs, transformative learning opportunities, and personal attention from dedicated faculty and staff. Our beautiful campus, an 80-acre arboretum with stunning lake views, is home to 2,600 undergraduate students and 200 graduate students. Founded in 1847, Carthage is consistently named a Best Midwestern College by The Princeton Review and a Most Innovative School by U.S. News & World Report. All Carthage employees play a vital part in the success of our students, as we work together to create an environment where all can achieve their true potential. Grow with Carthage. Carthage College is an equal opportunity employer (EOE) dedicated to the goal of building a culturally diverse community. We welcome applications from a broad spectrum of people, including members of ethnic minorities, women, veterans, and individuals with disabilities. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, gender expression, gender identity, sexual orientation, national origin, protected veteran status or status as an individual with a disability. 2001 Alford Park Drive Kenosha, WI 53140 (262) 551-8500 Contact Map & Directions Request Info Apply Visit Carthage Give Light that Travels | The Campaign For Carthage Athletics Bookstore Library/IT OneLogin The Bridge Virtual Tour Work at Carthage #carthageviews Instagram Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Merit Pages TikTok © Carthage College Privacy Policy Non-Discrimination Statement Policies Title IX This website uses cookies to measure traffic and improve your experience. Declining tracking cookies will set a single cookie to remember your preference. You can learn more by visiting our Privacy Policy . Accept Decline"
